The files in this directory are **derived works** — formalizations of the
textbook's statements and proofs — and are distributed under the same **GFDL
1.3** copyleft. Theorem statements are transcribed from the textbook; the bpa
proofs follow its arguments.

## What's here

| File | Chapter | Status |
|---|---|---|
| `sets.md` | 1 — Preliminaries (§1.2.1 Set Theory) | ✅ full transliteration; set algebra + De Morgan (14 theorems), verified pure |
| `groups.md` | 3 — Groups (Basic Properties) | ✅ 5 propositions + 5 exercises, verified pure |

The set theory rests on `std/set.bpa` (sets over an abstract `Universe` of
elements, fixed membershipwise, with extensionality). Every identity is proved
by the same recipe — extensionality → fix an element → unfold `member(x, ·)` →
one `[by tautology …]` — so the whole chapter is oracle-free.

The group theory rests on `std/group.bpa` (the group axioms as a reusable bpa
theory) and uses the `assoc` tactic (associativity-only reordering) for the
non-commutative rearrangements.

## What's deferred (the forcing-function backlog)

Most of the textbook needs machinery bpa does not yet have. Rather than skip
those exercises silently, each is listed in the relevant `.md` under a
`#### Solution` note stating exactly what it would require — a running backlog
of standard-library constructions that future chapters will motivate:

- a concrete **ℤ_n / U(n)** model (modular arithmetic as a group carrier),
- **finite sets + cardinality** (counting arguments, Cayley tables, Lagrange),
- **matrix / GLₙ** constructions and the reals,
- a **group power** `gⁿ` (recursive over a Nat exponent) for the ℕ-indexed
  exercises,
- **sets-of-sets / quotient structure + a relation sort** — Chapter 1's §1.2.3
  (equivalence relations ⟺ partitions) needs equivalence classes `[a]` and the
  partition `X = ⋃[x]`, which `std/set.bpa`'s flat `member : Universe → Set`
  model cannot express; and the **indexed families** `⋃ᵢ Aᵢ` / `⋂ᵢ Aᵢ` need a
  sort of finite sequences of `Set`.

Each is a self-contained addition; the translation grows as they land.
